From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:10:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Give the SAX reader MSXML's properties, limits and
 DTD handling.

Ported from the measured behaviour of the old tree's libxml2-based
reader (3d006c718c6, 010cc2744ad, 7525a31a253, 20b94d413ff) onto the
new parser:

- max-xml-size and max-element-depth stop the parse as each version
  does: MSXML 3 with E_ABORT and a formatted system error naming the
  limit, MSXML 6 with its own codes, at the positions Windows reports;
  a string input counts characters before MSXML 6, bytes after;
- baseURL and secureBaseURL are kept, and the identifiers of a
  declaration that has none are empty strings from MSXML 4.0 on;
- element declarations report their content model as written, and the
  entities a DTD declares are expanded where they are referenced;
- prohibit-dtd refuses a document type declaration.

saxpropprobe now differs from Windows in 32 lines instead of 399 and
saxdtdprobe in none instead of 19; the tests added pass on Windows 11.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

